00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:40,160
stab each other.

273
00:09:41,130 --> 00:09:42,450
You two are a terrible match.

274
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:45,590
Oh no.

275
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,490
We live so close.

276
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,120
What should I do?

277
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:53,590
Pick one more card, Auntie Duang.

278
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:56,990
This one.

279
00:10:01,730 --> 00:10:02,640
It says

280
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:04,500
you'll face karma

281
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,840
that can't be avoided.

282
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:09,190
You'll keep running into someone you hate!

283
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,190
Huh?

284
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,730
You have a person you hate?

285
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,270
All I see is people who hate you,

286
00:10:15,110 --> 00:10:16,640
cause you love gossiping about others.

287
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:17,940
Wow,

288
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,390
Mr. Community Relations Officer,

289
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:20,920
you're kind to others,

290
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:22,540
but mean to your mother?

291
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:23,910
True.

292
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:24,870
But wait,

293
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:27,160
the card says

294
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,360
this kind of person will live aimlessly,

295
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:30,440
with no clear goal.

296
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,460
Just living happily day by day.

297
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,630
Does this sound familiar, Mom?

298
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:39,160
That sounds like Dad.

299
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:42,100
Your dad?

300
00:10:42,130 --> 00:10:43,770
He's been gone for more than twenty years.

301
00:10:43,790 --> 00:10:44,760
He's not coming back.

302
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:48,830
The card says you'll get to meet him

303
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,190
really soon.

304
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,360
Hey, Mom!

305
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:58,070
I'll get to meet him, right?

306
00:10:58,710 --> 00:11:00,130
Mom, he's really coming back, right?

307
00:11:02,210 --> 00:11:03,420
No way.

308
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,240
He's already dead.

309
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:06,640
How do you know he's already dead?

310
00:11:06,690 --> 00:11:08,410
Dad just went to the market,

311
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:09,800
and then he just disappeared.

312
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:10,930
Maybe...

313
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:11,870
he just got lost.

314
00:11:11,890 --> 00:11:13,080
For twenty years?

315
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:13,620
Mm.

316
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,120
Did he go to Mars or something?

317
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:16,300
Hey, seriously,

318
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:17,610
are you still hoping he'll come back?

319
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:19,010
Because to me, he's long gone.

320
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:19,740
No!

321
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,400
Dead!

322
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:25,380
Boys...

323
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,870
Ugh, what's wrong with you guys?

324
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:29,100
Every time their dad is mentioned,
they act like this.

325
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:35,630
The security cameras are broken.

326
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,690
Grandma's photo is no good.

327
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,080
Alright,

328
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,810
let's knock on every door in this dorm,

329
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:45,810
so we'll know who is
Grandma Gaysorn's relative.

330
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,590
Hello, I'm the new owner of this dorm...

331
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:56,080
Take out the trash for me.

332
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:02,490
Hello!

333
00:12:02,510 --> 00:12:04,180
- Oh!
- Whoa, whoa!

334
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,580
Oh, Dobby...

335
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,480
Hello, I'm the new owner.
Grandpa's grandson.

336
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,560
Well, I...

337
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,540
- Hello.
- Hello.

338
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,430
Hey!

339
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,660
- Don't close the door yet!
- Whoa!

340
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:24,700
Dobby, Dobby, Dobby!

341
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,310
Dobby!

342
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:28,780
Dobby. Dobby!

343
00:12:31,070 --> 00:12:32,200
- Hello.
- Oh, hello.

344
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,550
Khaidao.

345
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:34,870
A Rottweiler...

346
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:36,550
Oh, don't worry. He's friendly.

347
00:12:36,690 --> 00:12:37,840
- It's baring its teeth, though!
- Khaidao, dear.

348
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:39,040
Well, he's smiling.

349
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:40,400
- Smiling?
- He's actually friendly.

350
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:41,510
I can even let go of the leash.

351
00:12:41,530 --> 00:12:42,000
- Friendly?
- Huh?

352
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:42,680
Don't let go!

353
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,550
Whoa. Khaidao! Khaidao! Khaidao!

354
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:46,400
Khaidao! Those!

355
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:47,720
- Those balls aren't dog toys!
- Khaidao!

356
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:48,990
How are you feeling, Dobby?

357
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,750
Ouch, my balls!

358
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,240
Ow...

359
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:56,850
- Ow, it stings.
- Sorry, sorry.

360
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,770
Ow...

361
00:13:01,850 --> 00:13:03,130
I have fought many battles,

362
00:13:03,270 --> 00:13:05,170
yet never have I seen a comrade

363
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,650
bitten in the balls like this.

364
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,750
Well, there's me!

365
00:13:08,770 --> 00:13:10,110
Come on...

366
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:13,130
What are you laughing at, Grandpa?

367
00:13:13,590 --> 00:13:15,070
I'm like this because of you!

368
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:16,630
Ouch!

369
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:18,490
Oh, it stings.

370
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:21,710
Hey, Dobby,

371
00:13:21,730 --> 00:13:22,960
don't you think that's a bit weird?

372
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:24,420
Why do the people in this dorm

373
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:25,790
hate you so much?

374
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,500
- Right?
- Yeah.

375
00:13:27,710 --> 00:13:29,330
I already said that

376
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:30,950
I won't sell this dorm.

377
00:13:30,970 --> 00:13:31,800
That's right.

378
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,790
Maybe it is because of me.

379
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:38,800
Back when I was still alive...

380
00:13:42,190 --> 00:13:44,620
When they saw the photo
they were looking for was ruined,

381
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:46,850
they went around
knocking on our tenants' doors.

382
00:13:46,870 --> 00:13:48,330
I happened to hear that...

383
00:13:48,470 --> 00:13:49,520
Yes?

384
00:13:51,690 --> 00:13:52,600
Your hair smells good.

385
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:54,570
Want to smell something else, then?

386
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,030
I'm sorry, I got carried away.

387
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:56,980
Well...

388
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,290
they were pretty far away,
so I couldn't hear them.

389
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,400
Maybe

390
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:03,470
he went around introducing himself
as the new owner.

391
00:14:03,830 --> 00:14:05,550
Building a good relationship
with his tenants!

392
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,470
Mr. Dobby, how nice of you.

393
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,230
No way.

394
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:12,280
Someone as ungrateful as him?

395
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,450
You really think he'd think of others?

396
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:14,450
Can't be.

397
00:14:14,470 --> 00:14:15,410
Then, how about this?

398
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:17,700
If you want to know their plans,
it's very simple.

399
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:19,280
We can invite them to a party,

400
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:21,600
get them drunk, then ask them.

401
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:22,980
Whoa...

402
00:14:23,090 --> 00:14:24,540
That's a good plan, Dum.

403
00:14:24,710 --> 00:14:25,520
Despicable!

404
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:27,410
That's my little brother.

405
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,540
Well done.

406
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:30,430
I don't know if I should be proud…

407
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,070
Hey!

408
00:14:32,090 --> 00:14:34,160
So, the reason
everyone in this dorm hates you

409
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,220
is because your grandpa

410
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:36,240
told them that

411
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:37,780
you and your mother abandoned him?!

412
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,990
Exactly!

413
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,680
Just think about it.

414
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,520
Grandpa went around badmouthing my mother,

415
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,040
saying that whenever he came to visit,

416
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,740
she'd drive him away like a dog.

417
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:47,150
When in reality,

418
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,710
Grandpa never even bothered with her.

419
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:50,860
He never came to see her
or his own grandson!

420
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:52,760
Let that sit with you.

421
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:53,940
Why, though?

422
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,500
I was lonely.

423
00:14:55,530 --> 00:14:57,500
I wanted some attention,

424
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:59,150
so I made up some stories.

425
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:01,230
- Stories? Stories, my foot...
- Hey, hey!

426
00:15:02,430 --> 00:15:03,600
Ouch, it hurts!

427
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:04,260
Dax!

428
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,340
Hey, sorry, sorry.

429
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:06,490
But can you stop fighting?

430
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:07,970
Alright, I'll stop.

431
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:10,640
We have to think about
what we're going to do next.

432
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:11,920
The cameras are broken.

433
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:13,450
Grandma Gaysorn's photo is no good.

434
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,800
Everyone in this dorm hates you, too.

435
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,350
What should we do now?

436
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:19,170
There is a way.

437
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:19,960
Hm?

438
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:21,350
Hm?

439
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:22,270
You know full well

440
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:23,620
that the tenants

441
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,740
love Danis.

442
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,500
Just get Danis on your side.

443
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:28,990
Everything will be easier.

444
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:30,800
As if it were that easy, Grandpa!

445
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,170
You have to picture this.

446
00:15:32,190 --> 00:15:34,000
Danis hates my guts.

447
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:34,880
Very much.

448
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,300
Why would she help me?!

449
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,240
Come on!

450
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:44,810
Huh?!

451
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,890
You're hosting a welcome party for me?

452
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:48,100
Yes.

453
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,200
Are you okay?

454
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,780
Of course!

455
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,760
It's not your concern.

456
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,290
Just get to the point.

457
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,730
Well...I feel bad
for what I did this morning.

458
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:02,570
I judged you too harshly.

459
00:16:02,590 --> 00:16:04,710
We have to take care of the dorm together,

460
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:08,890
so I wanted to
get to know you better. Yeah?

461
00:16:14,370 --> 00:16:15,790
Um, alright.

462
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,640
Then, I'll see you tomorrow.

463
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,920
Is your mustache crooked?

464
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,630
Mm.

465
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,360
Your mustache, not your eyebrow.

466
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,480
I'll see you tomorrow.

467
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:29,760
Go check.

468
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,110
Don't forget.

469
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:32,470
See you tomorrow.

470
00:16:34,890 --> 00:16:35,560
Dobby.

471
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:36,160
Huh?

472
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:37,280
I think something is off.

473
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,440
She was just yelling at us this morning.

474
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:40,280
But now she's hosting a party for us?

475
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,120
It does seem off.

476
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:43,360
But we don't have a choice, do we?

477
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:44,570
We have to risk it.

478
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,490
You're right...

479
00:16:45,610 --> 00:16:47,070
If you want a puppy,

480
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,210
you'll have to venture into a dog's den.

481
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:51,070
Was it not "a tiger's den"?

482
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:52,680
Well, she bites back like a dog.

483
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:53,320
I see.

484
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:55,110
So it should be a dog, Grandpa.

485
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,560
[The D Dorm]

486
00:17:04,579 --> 00:17:06,000
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

487
00:17:06,510 --> 00:17:07,880
Hello, Mom.

488
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:10,200
Oh, wow...

489
00:17:10,839 --> 00:17:11,880
Today,

490
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:14,200
I'm doing fittings
for the actors from one31.

491
00:17:14,730 --> 00:17:16,079
I'll get to meet Bie today.

492
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,579
Would you like his autograph?

493
00:17:18,599 --> 00:17:20,440
I don't want his autograph.

494
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:22,839
I want his leg hair.

495
00:17:22,859 --> 00:17:24,140
He was at the temple for so long,

496
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,200
I bet his leg hair is definitely sacred.

497
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:28,359
Okay, Mom.

498
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,810
I'll get going.

499
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:30,720
Mm.

500
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:31,220
See you.

501
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,300
- Okay.
- Wait, Dolly.

502
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,720
If you want to stay safe…

503
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:36,940
why don't you let the cards guide you?

504
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:41,220
- A truck could flatten you as you walk.
- Hey...

505
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:43,230
Trust me,

506
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,190
you never know when bad luck will strike.

507
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:48,560
Ow!

508
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,590
What's this, Auntie?!

509
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:56,520
Oh! Venerable Salty Grandpa's
phallic amulet.

510
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:57,500
Sadhu. Oh dear.

511
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:58,460
Pass it here.

512
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,000
Oh, I thought I'd lost it. Gosh.

513
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:03,190
Found it. Sadhu.

514
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:03,950
Mom!

515
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,100
- Oh...
- Oh, dear.

516
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,050
Sadhu, sadhu.

517
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,140
I think you should
let the cards guide you.

518
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,320
How can you be

519
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,000
this unlucky every day?

520
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:17,040
Mom,

521
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:18,380
why are the dogs barking?

522
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:19,670
They're barking at your brother.

523
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,580
- Hey!
- Whoa!

524
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:24,890
Um...you're a cop.

525
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:25,630
What's this costume?

526
00:18:25,650 --> 00:18:27,170
Today, the community relations officers

527
00:18:27,190 --> 00:18:29,920
have an activity to promote waste sorting.

528
00:18:29,930 --> 00:18:32,210
Oh...my brother.

529
00:18:32,870 --> 00:18:33,450
What are you laughing at?

530
00:18:34,290 --> 00:18:35,640
We still have to talk
about yesterday.

531
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,320
Who'd want to talk to
someone so narrow-minded?

532
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:40,960
You can't even forgive

533
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:41,980
your own father.

534
00:18:42,010 --> 00:18:43,740
Stop defending that selfish man!

535
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,350
How did you know Dad was selfish?!

536
00:18:46,590 --> 00:18:48,020
You were only four then.

537
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,610
Probably couldn't even wipe your own butt.

538
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,450
You were still in Mom's womb,
squishing her large intestine.

539
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:53,940
What would you know?

540
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,670
All you did was lie there
talking to Mom's poop!

541
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,040
Hey, boys,

542
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:00,110
don't talk about food while
someone is eating poop.

543
00:19:00,130 --> 00:19:01,040
- Oops.
- Oh.

544
00:19:02,890 --> 00:19:04,170
Eating food. Sorry.

545
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:06,790
Dolly, you should go to work.

546
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:09,170
- Mom, look at him.
- Go to work.

547
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:10,640
Sadhu,

548
00:19:10,660 --> 00:19:12,620
I hope the cards Dawin read

549
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:14,680
mean Dad is coming back.

550
00:19:15,670 --> 00:19:17,400
I want to see someone die of frustration.

551
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,720
- Where the hell are you going?!
- Dollar, Dollar.

552
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:25,310
Go get changed.

553
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:27,700
Can you also go buy
a wealth-beckoning goddess with me?

554
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:29,790
I want to give it to
the coffee shop owner downstairs.

555
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:31,310
But didn't Dawin's cards

556
00:19:31,410 --> 00:19:32,890
say that you aren't compatible with him?

557
00:19:32,910 --> 00:19:33,770
Dollar,

558
00:19:33,790 --> 00:19:35,230
we're neighboring shops.

559
00:19:35,470 --> 00:19:37,370
It's good to be kind.

560
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,910
Our fortunes could change.

561
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,040
They couldn't, Auntie.

562
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,960
The cards clearly said

563
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:44,890
your luck

564
00:19:44,910 --> 00:19:47,690
will stab, stab, stab the other person!

565
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:48,360
Oh...

566
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,270
Go get changed. Hurry.

567
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:54,300
Still staring? Are you gonna buy it or not?

568
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:56,900
What's it gonna be?

569
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:07,680
Whoa,

570
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:10,030
that face card
pierced through the smoke.

571
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:17,200
[Drip, occupation: coffee shop owner]

572
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,230
The grilled chicken smells good,

573
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,890
but...the smoke is burning my eyes.

574
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,870
Then why are you still standing here?

575
00:20:25,790 --> 00:20:27,200
So, just one skewer?

576
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:28,220
Yes.

577
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,400
Twenty baht.

578
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:30,520
No QR payments.

579
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:31,490
No transfers.

580
00:20:31,510 --> 00:20:32,820
No large bills.

581
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:34,300
Yes.

582
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:42,280
Aw,

583
00:20:42,810 --> 00:20:44,500
cool but starving, huh?

584
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,120
Auntie Aoy.

585
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:47,720
Yes?

586
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:48,510
I'll pay for him.

587
00:20:49,490 --> 00:20:50,120
Huh?

588
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,060
It's okay.

589
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:52,310
It's on me.

590
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:57,540
Thank you.

591
00:21:02,310 --> 00:21:03,530
What's going on?

592
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:09,920
What?

593
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:10,920
Hey!

594
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:11,870
Hey!

595
00:21:12,110 --> 00:21:12,810
Wait!

596
00:21:12,950 --> 00:21:13,820
Hey!

597
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:16,760
Middle-class people are so kind.

598
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:24,350
Gosh!

599
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,680
Your chicken tastes even better
than Gordon's.

600
00:21:26,790 --> 00:21:27,590
What Don?

601
00:21:27,610 --> 00:21:29,140
If you mean Don Chedi,
of course it's better.

602
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:30,520
I used Bang Tan's recipe.

603
00:21:31,130 --> 00:21:32,300
You're amazing, Auntie.

604
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,030
Cheers!

605
00:21:36,050 --> 00:21:37,150
Cheers!

606
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,700
Let me join in, too.

607
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:39,510
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

608
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:40,160
Oh...

609
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,080
Are you trying to speedrun drinking?

610
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:43,130
Everyone else drinks from glasses,

611
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:45,090
but you drink from a vase.
You really wanna drink, huh?

612
00:21:45,570 --> 00:21:46,330
Hey!

613
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:48,370
There goes our drink, ugh...

614
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,350
Back in my day, there were no glasses.

615
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,490
If I don't drink from a vase,

616
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:53,840
what should I drink from?

617
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,520
Hey,

618
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:56,910
why are you drinking water?

619
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:59,410
Let's indulge in some liquor.

620
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:00,230
Come on!

621
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,650
Don't!

622
00:22:01,670 --> 00:22:03,880
You call this indulging in liquor?
You're pouring it over my head!

623
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:06,220
You go drink with them, yeah?

624
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:08,900
Well, I... I can't indulge in liquor.

625
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,600
I'm allergic.

626
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:14,210
You can have Dennis do whatever you want,

627
00:22:14,230 --> 00:22:16,480
but do not let her drink.

628
00:22:20,390 --> 00:22:22,360
Try talking to her about a badminton court.

629
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:23,930
She has wanted it for a long time now.

630
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:25,910
If you say it,

631
00:22:25,930 --> 00:22:28,250
you might win her over,

632
00:22:28,270 --> 00:22:30,800
and maybe she will work with you.

633
00:22:33,530 --> 00:22:34,420
Um, hey...

634
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:35,360
Hm?

635
00:22:36,010 --> 00:22:37,710
Do you see the free space over there?

636
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,070
There.

637
00:22:40,610 --> 00:22:41,260
Mm,

638
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:41,840
I do.

639
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:42,800
Well, I don't.

640
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:44,090
What?

641
00:22:44,110 --> 00:22:45,200
But you asked me.

642
00:22:46,070 --> 00:22:47,490
Hey...do not joke around.

643
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,860
Just kidding.
Maybe I'm drinking too much.

644
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,330
I see.

645
00:22:51,350 --> 00:22:52,650
Hey, look there.

646
00:22:52,670 --> 00:22:53,720
I just think that

647
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:55,160
if we leave it like that,

648
00:22:55,170 --> 00:22:56,500
the area will go to waste.

649
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:59,060
But we can build a badminton court

650
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,080
so the tenants

651
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:01,980
can exercise down there.

652
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:02,620
What do you think?

653
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:03,640
Hey!

654
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:05,620
You want to build a badminton court, too?

655
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:07,130
I had the same idea!

656
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:09,580
- See? See?
- Wow!

657
00:23:12,710 --> 00:23:13,480
Oh, oh.

658
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:15,320
You see, we're here

659
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:17,330
to party today, right?

660
00:23:17,350 --> 00:23:19,250
Let's not talk business yet, yeah?

661
00:23:19,270 --> 00:23:20,230
I think...

662
00:23:20,250 --> 00:23:23,120
we should get to know each other better.

663
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:24,070
Sounds good?

664
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:25,200
I like your idea.

665
00:23:25,220 --> 00:23:25,960
Right?!

666
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:27,110
Exactly.

667
00:23:27,130 --> 00:23:29,380
They say people grow closer

668
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:30,730
when they drink together a lot.

669
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,330
- Yes.
- Don't stop drinking.

670
00:23:32,590 --> 00:23:33,960
- Cheers!
- True!

671
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:35,850
- Cheers!
- Yes, cheers!

672
00:23:35,870 --> 00:23:37,030
Me, too.

673
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:41,430
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

674
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:44,760
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

675
00:23:46,810 --> 00:23:49,670
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

676
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,390
Cheers!

677
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,520
Well, they are close.

678
00:23:58,990 --> 00:24:00,640
Close to sleeping like a log.

679
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:03,100
I think...

680
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:05,390
what happens next might not be very fun.

681
00:24:05,730 --> 00:24:07,130
I cannot stay here anymore.

682
00:24:07,150 --> 00:24:08,080
I should leave.

683
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:09,710
Water...

684
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:11,280
Whoa!

685
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:15,680
Come closer. I'm gonna whisper.

686
00:24:15,940 --> 00:24:17,220
Whisper in my ear.

687
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:18,590
- Now's the time.
- Mm.

688
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:19,470
They're drunk.

689
00:24:19,490 --> 00:24:21,660
You can ask them
what you wanna know. Go on.

690
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:22,770
Oh, that's true.

691
00:24:22,790 --> 00:24:23,380
Yeah.

692
00:24:23,450 --> 00:24:24,400
Mr. Dobby.

693
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:25,420
Mr. Dobby!

694
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:26,930
Mr. Dobby...

695
00:24:27,210 --> 00:24:27,940
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

696
00:24:28,990 --> 00:24:30,500
It's nothing, Mr. Dobby!

697
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,730
Why did you knock on
the tenants' door?

698
00:24:32,910 --> 00:24:34,360
What were you talking about?

699
00:24:34,910 --> 00:24:35,590
Hm?

700
00:24:35,690 --> 00:24:36,480
Oh...

701
00:24:37,790 --> 00:24:38,530
I was...

702
00:24:39,020 --> 00:24:39,930
I was...

703
00:24:40,340 --> 00:24:41,250
I was...

704
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,490
What were you talking about?

705
00:24:43,610 --> 00:24:45,370
Go make me another drink!

706
00:24:46,550 --> 00:24:48,000
Man, I'm feeling so good right now...

707
00:24:48,010 --> 00:24:49,330
Go make me another one!

708
00:24:49,690 --> 00:24:51,280
Maybe he hasn't hit his limit yet,

709
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:52,770
but don't worry.

710
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:53,170
Mm.

711
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,810
I'll make him a drink.

712
00:24:55,830 --> 00:24:57,410
I'll make it strong.

713
00:24:57,600 --> 00:25:00,380
When he's wasted,

714
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,020
- you can ask him again, alright?
- Right.

715
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:02,690
Mm, okay.

716
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:04,560
- Leave it to me. Don't worry.
- Okay, okay.

717
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,140
Let me make you a drink.

718
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:07,960
Mr. Dobby, he will make it for you.

719
00:25:08,190 --> 00:25:10,270
Hey...why are there so many glasses?

720
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:12,700
- It's right here.
- Oh.

721
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:13,450
Okay.

722
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:15,270
- Can you do it?
- Ah, easy.

723
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:19,220
Hey, hey, hey, are you good?

724
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:20,640
Alcohol is weird.

725
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:22,260
I drink through my mouth,
but my legs stop working.

726
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:24,160
I only have two legs,
how are they tangled?

727
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:28,650
- Hey!
- Whoa!

728
00:25:30,630 --> 00:25:32,160
That's enough, my beloved brother.

729
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:35,160
He hasn't even drunk that much,
and he's already wasted.

730
00:25:35,690 --> 00:25:37,300
If you make him drink any more,

731
00:25:37,330 --> 00:25:39,380
he might die of shock.

732
00:25:39,700 --> 00:25:41,220
Why be scared of something so silly?

733
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:43,850
Hey, kiddo!

734
00:25:43,870 --> 00:25:44,870
If you are scared of dying,

735
00:25:44,890 --> 00:25:46,200
go back to bed, coward!

736
00:25:46,700 --> 00:25:47,680
Hey!

737
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:48,880
Who said that?!

738
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,920
How dare you slander
your dear big brother like this?!

739
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:54,600
Let go.

740
00:25:55,190 --> 00:25:56,920
Big brother this, big brother that.

741
00:25:56,940 --> 00:25:59,050
You were born
five seconds before me.

742
00:25:59,070 --> 00:26:00,440
You think you're better than me, prick?!

743
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:03,600
You dare call me "prick"?!

744
00:26:03,620 --> 00:26:05,470
I've argued with Dad for days on end.

745
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:06,950
Oh, wow!

746
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:10,040
- Hey, hey, hey, wait!
- Whoa!

747
00:26:10,620 --> 00:26:11,260
- Hey!
- You want some?

748
00:26:11,290 --> 00:26:12,350
You want this, Daeng?

749
00:26:12,370 --> 00:26:14,130
Are you challenging me?!

750
00:26:14,150 --> 00:26:16,610
I've never punched anyone
in my twenty-five years of life.

751
00:26:16,630 --> 00:26:17,630
Come! Bring it!

752
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:23,660
I saw that he opened his new coffee shop,

753
00:26:23,730 --> 00:26:24,970
so we should support him.

754
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:26,380
- That's right, Auntie.
- Since we're neighbors.

755
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,980
- We should be kind to each other.
- Wow...

756
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:29,100
Oh!

757
00:26:29,120 --> 00:26:30,410
So many customers.

758
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:32,170
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

759
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:35,160
Hello,

760
00:26:35,450 --> 00:26:37,000
I'm Auntie Duang.

761
00:26:37,020 --> 00:26:38,400
I own the restaurant upstairs.

762
00:26:38,530 --> 00:26:39,490
This is Dawin.

763
00:26:39,510 --> 00:26:40,730
He lives here, too.

764
00:26:41,310 --> 00:26:41,790
Hello.

765
00:26:41,810 --> 00:26:43,120
- Hello, hello.
- Hello.

766
00:26:43,770 --> 00:26:46,080
I brought you a gift for your grand opening.

767
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,190
Cool!

768
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:49,960
Is this the new Art Toy collection?

769
00:26:50,390 --> 00:26:51,330
How cute.

770
00:26:51,770 --> 00:26:52,890
No...

771
00:26:52,910 --> 00:26:53,760
This is Nang Kwak.

772
00:26:53,780 --> 00:26:55,200
Nang...Guac?

773
00:26:55,220 --> 00:26:56,220
Nang Kwak,
a wealth-beckoning goddess.

774
00:26:56,360 --> 00:26:57,440
Nang Guac?

775
00:26:59,280 --> 00:27:00,570
Nang Kwak.

776
00:27:00,850 --> 00:27:01,390
Guac!

777
00:27:01,740 --> 00:27:02,280
Kwak!

778
00:27:02,590 --> 00:27:03,260
Guac.

779
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:04,390
"Kwak," as in...

780
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:06,760
Quick, quick, come here!

781
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:09,030
Business will be booming!
Come, customers, come!

782
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:09,950
Oh!

783
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:10,450
"Kwak," like beckoning!

784
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:11,770
Yes, Nang Kwak!

785
00:27:11,790 --> 00:27:12,860
Oh, I get it now.

786
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:13,610
Mm.

787
00:27:13,630 --> 00:27:15,250
Take good care of her.

788
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:16,790
She can bring you luck.

789
00:27:16,810 --> 00:27:18,120
Oh, then...

790
00:27:18,140 --> 00:27:19,810
please tell them I can't wait to meet Lux.

791
00:27:19,830 --> 00:27:21,980
I'll tell Lux that you said that.

792
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:23,510
- Hey!
- Hey!

793
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,540
No, this is mine.

794
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:27,440
"Luck," like
"May great fortune be with you."

795
00:27:27,580 --> 00:27:28,580
Oh.

796
00:27:28,670 --> 00:27:29,470
Then...

797
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:31,040
please thank Grace for me.

798
00:27:31,060 --> 00:27:32,410
I'll tell her that.

799
00:27:32,430 --> 00:27:33,930
- Hey!
- Hey!

800
00:27:34,150 --> 00:27:34,920
Never mind.

801
00:27:34,940 --> 00:27:35,940
Just take good care of her.

802
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,480
Wherever she goes, business will be good.

803
00:27:37,780 --> 00:27:38,720
Okay.

804
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:41,300
Do you really not know,
or are you just messing with her?

805
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:42,520
I'm not messing with her.

806
00:27:43,420 --> 00:27:45,610
I just came back from overseas.

807
00:27:45,850 --> 00:27:47,200
I still can't remember...

808
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:49,280
some words.

809
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,000
- Mm...
- Mm...

810
00:27:52,590 --> 00:27:55,190
It's your first day, and you
already have this many customers.

811
00:27:55,210 --> 00:27:56,480
You're good at this, huh?

812
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:57,500
I'll order too, then.

813
00:27:58,190 --> 00:27:59,190
One for me

814
00:27:59,210 --> 00:28:00,090
and one for Dawin.

815
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:04,630
Of course, but...

816
00:28:05,290 --> 00:28:06,610
you'll have to wait for a while.

817
00:28:06,650 --> 00:28:08,420
I'm about to make...

818
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:10,190
my first customer's order.

819
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:12,600
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

820
00:28:13,010 --> 00:28:14,680
I've been waiting for an hour now.

821
00:28:14,910 --> 00:28:15,910
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

822
00:28:17,010 --> 00:28:18,520
When will we get ours, then?

823
00:28:19,570 --> 00:28:20,520
You'll get them today.

824
00:28:21,070 --> 00:28:23,290
You'll be my last order for today.

825
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:25,590
Today, I'll only sell ten cups.

826
00:28:25,850 --> 00:28:27,390
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

827
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:39,070
Ugh...when will I get my coffee?

828
00:28:42,510 --> 00:28:44,090
Calm down, Auntie.

829
00:28:44,560 --> 00:28:45,820
Good coffee

830
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:46,840
has to be ground slowly

831
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:50,660
to bring out its full flavor and aroma.

832
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Why don't you get a grinder?

833
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:54,100
It's faster and more efficient.

834
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:55,570
I don't want speed.

835
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,570
What I want is the joy I get

836
00:28:57,590 --> 00:29:00,600
from hearing the sound
of coffee beans being slowly ground.

837
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Slowly ground...

838
00:29:02,110 --> 00:29:03,760
Crunch...crunch...

839
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,710
Crunch...crunch...

840
00:29:06,100 --> 00:29:07,810
Crunch...crunch...

841
00:29:08,280 --> 00:29:09,800
Crunch...crunch...

842
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:12,850
This is the joy of life.

843
00:29:13,610 --> 00:29:16,320
Oh, do you feel the same way, Auntie?

844
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:17,400
It's not my idea,

845
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,370
but my husband's.

846
00:29:19,010 --> 00:29:20,210
When he was chopping crispy pork belly,

847
00:29:20,220 --> 00:29:21,890
he said exactly those words!

848
00:29:21,910 --> 00:29:23,710
You are very lucky

849
00:29:23,730 --> 00:29:24,890
to have such a cool husband.

850
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:26,640
What a role model.

851
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:28,590
Role model, my foot!

852
00:29:28,610 --> 00:29:29,770
I don't want the coffee anymore.

853
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:31,450
It reminds me of my husband!

854
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:32,530
So irritating!

855
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,870
Give this back to me!

856
00:29:35,930 --> 00:29:36,550
No more!

857
00:29:36,570 --> 00:29:37,760
It'd be better if she stayed at my place!

858
00:29:37,780 --> 00:29:38,510
Wait, Auntie Duang.

859
00:29:38,530 --> 00:29:40,100
You haven't paid yet!

860
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:42,410
Ugh...I'm having bad luck again!

861
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,710
Bring me two cups.

862
00:29:45,220 --> 00:29:46,000
I'll drink them myself.

863
00:29:46,150 --> 00:29:47,080
Um...

864
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,410
Please wait a moment.

865
00:29:49,430 --> 00:29:50,760
Three more orders to go.

866
00:29:56,320 --> 00:29:57,600
Can I change my mind?

867
00:29:58,310 --> 00:29:59,940
Just wait a little longer.

868
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:01,210
Really.

869
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:02,640
Is that so?

870
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:03,610
Yes.

871
00:30:03,900 --> 00:30:05,030
One moment.

872
00:30:05,050 --> 00:30:06,200
- Hey!
- Calm down!

873
00:30:09,940 --> 00:30:10,590
Ugh!

874
00:30:11,350 --> 00:30:13,230
Stop. Let's get back to drinking, alright?

875
00:30:13,260 --> 00:30:14,110
- Alright?
- No!

876
00:30:14,300 --> 00:30:15,230
Where did you learn to box?

877
00:30:15,250 --> 00:30:16,130
I threw punch after punch,

878
00:30:16,150 --> 00:30:17,330
and you dodged every damn one!

879
00:30:17,350 --> 00:30:18,350
That's enough, Guard Dum.

880
00:30:18,370 --> 00:30:19,520
Handyman Daeng, stop.

881
00:30:19,540 --> 00:30:21,220
Let me get one clean punch in, then.

882
00:30:28,300 --> 00:30:29,710
You dare fight back
against your own brother?

883
00:30:29,730 --> 00:30:31,020
No, no, no more.

884
00:30:31,040 --> 00:30:32,840
- Stop fighting...
- I'm older than you, you scoundrel!

885
00:30:32,860 --> 00:30:33,910
You calling me a scoundrel

886
00:30:33,930 --> 00:30:35,640
makes my blood boil, you bastard!

887
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:38,850
- You want some? Come here!
- You want this, huh?!

888
00:30:38,870 --> 00:30:39,870
Hey, stop!

889
00:30:39,900 --> 00:30:40,530
Calm down!

890
00:30:40,550 --> 00:30:41,050
That's enough.

891
00:30:41,070 --> 00:30:42,190
Ugh, then you stop them!

892
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:44,030
I'm done. I'm tired, alright?!

893
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:45,500
Go ahead and deal with them!

894
00:30:45,650 --> 00:30:46,420
Hey!

895
00:30:46,960 --> 00:30:47,830
They're fighting,

896
00:30:47,850 --> 00:30:48,500
and you're...

897
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:49,810
just going to let me stop them by myself?

898
00:30:49,990 --> 00:30:50,610
What?

899
00:30:50,630 --> 00:30:51,250
- Hey, what?
- Hey...

900
00:30:51,260 --> 00:30:52,400
- What?
- See?!

901
00:30:52,530 --> 00:30:54,140
You made Ms. Danis mad!

902
00:30:54,460 --> 00:30:55,570
As your big brother,

903
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:57,230
I order you to apologize to her!

904
00:30:57,260 --> 00:30:58,260
Big brother?

905
00:30:58,340 --> 00:30:59,430
I don't like the sound of that.

906
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:00,890
I'll tell you this, then!

907
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,080
You're only older

908
00:31:02,090 --> 00:31:04,120
because you were closer to Mom's coochie.

909
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:07,250
That's why you slipped out first!

910
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:09,330
I slipped out before you

911
00:31:09,520 --> 00:31:10,860
because you were so big!

912
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:12,480
You had to squeeze through!

913
00:31:12,490 --> 00:31:13,070
Like this!

914
00:31:13,610 --> 00:31:16,870
- Hey, don't...
- Well, if I came out before you,

915
00:31:16,890 --> 00:31:17,890
you'd slip out...

916
00:31:17,900 --> 00:31:19,310
like you were on
the slides at Siam Amazing Park.

917
00:31:19,590 --> 00:31:22,380
But I didn't do that,
'cause I love Mom very much.

918
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:24,480
I was clinging to Mom's ovaries like this.

919
00:31:24,500 --> 00:31:25,500
When the doctor grabbed my leg,

920
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:27,080
I kicked him away!

921
00:31:27,100 --> 00:31:28,180
Hey!

922
00:31:28,200 --> 00:31:30,590
Can you two stop arguing
about your mother's coochie?

923
00:31:30,610 --> 00:31:32,060
- You...
- Let's leave it at that for now.

924
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:33,150
But you and I!

925
00:31:33,170 --> 00:31:34,620
- Come here!
- Bring it!

926
00:31:34,830 --> 00:31:36,160
Come on, then!

927
00:31:36,180 --> 00:31:36,920
Hey...

928
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:37,930
- Bring it!
- Why are you blocking me?!

929
00:31:37,940 --> 00:31:38,880
You two... Hey!

930
00:31:38,900 --> 00:31:40,320
- Ow... Hey, you!
- Do it, then!

931
00:31:40,340 --> 00:31:41,550
- Wait! Wait!
- Bring it on!

932
00:31:41,570 --> 00:31:42,440
Hey...

933
00:31:42,470 --> 00:31:43,300
Hey, wait...

934
00:31:43,310 --> 00:31:43,690
Wait...

935
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:49,000
Didn't you say you were allergic?

936
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:50,110
Who?

937
00:31:50,290 --> 00:31:51,740
Someone like me

938
00:31:51,760 --> 00:31:54,010
doesn't go down that easily!

939
00:31:57,220 --> 00:31:59,310
- Oh, crap...
- Oh, crap...

940
00:32:00,740 --> 00:32:02,520
Mom.

941
00:32:03,790 --> 00:32:05,430
I heard there's a new coffee shop.

942
00:32:05,450 --> 00:32:06,230
How does it taste?

943
00:32:06,250 --> 00:32:07,450
Don't know. I didn't have any.

944
00:32:07,460 --> 00:32:09,090
Go ask Dawin instead.

945
00:32:09,110 --> 00:32:10,080
He drank two cups.

946
00:32:11,500 --> 00:32:12,700
He took quite a while.

947
00:32:12,930 --> 00:32:14,060
Pretty nice.

948
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:15,200
Pretty strong.

949
00:32:15,230 --> 00:32:16,850
Very strong!

950
00:32:18,330 --> 00:32:18,970
Hey,

951
00:32:18,990 --> 00:32:21,070
don't buy from him or hang around him.

952
00:32:21,090 --> 00:32:22,320
I just don't like him.

953
00:32:22,340 --> 00:32:23,600
Why, though?

954
00:32:23,910 --> 00:32:24,680
What did he do to you?

955
00:32:24,690 --> 00:32:25,740
He reminds me of your dad.

956
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:26,750
Huh?

957
00:32:26,770 --> 00:32:29,020
He takes an hour to make a single drink.

958
00:32:29,040 --> 00:32:29,860
He likes

959
00:32:29,870 --> 00:32:31,770
the sound of the coffee beans
cracking as he grinds them.

960
00:32:31,790 --> 00:32:32,930
He sells ten cups of coffee a day.

961
00:32:32,940 --> 00:32:33,800
He'll be rich real soon.

962
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:35,320
Hey, Mom,

963
00:32:35,340 --> 00:32:36,420
you're judging him

964
00:32:36,430 --> 00:32:38,330
just because he lives a slow life like Dad?

965
00:32:38,510 --> 00:32:39,880
He didn't do anything wrong.

966
00:32:40,300 --> 00:32:42,510
He was just doing what he enjoys.

967
00:32:42,990 --> 00:32:44,560
He isn't causing trouble for anyone.

968
00:32:45,900 --> 00:32:47,920
Really?
Or have you never seen it before?

969
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:52,090
I saw Mom and Dad arguing
about this all the time.

970
00:32:52,110 --> 00:32:53,270
Suddenly, Dad disappeared.

971
00:32:53,410 --> 00:32:54,890
He probably lives a slow life somewhere.

972
00:32:54,910 --> 00:32:57,010
He left Mom and me to struggle.

973
00:32:57,110 --> 00:32:57,920
And did you know

974
00:32:58,500 --> 00:32:59,480
how your mother...

975
00:32:59,550 --> 00:33:00,710
had to work hard

976
00:33:00,720 --> 00:33:02,560
to provide for you
while she was pregnant?

977
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:05,180
Did you see

978
00:33:05,670 --> 00:33:07,380
Dad leave and just drift through life?

979
00:33:10,300 --> 00:33:12,000
I know you're angry,

980
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:15,280
but don't try to make me
hate Dad like you do, okay?

981
00:33:15,980 --> 00:33:17,450
You can think whatever you want.

982
00:33:17,910 --> 00:33:19,330
But our family

983
00:33:19,490 --> 00:33:20,640
doesn't need him!

984
00:33:21,670 --> 00:33:23,240
I'll take care of you and Mom.

985
00:33:25,840 --> 00:33:26,910
Dawin,

986
00:33:26,930 --> 00:33:28,200
can you read my fortune?

987
00:33:29,100 --> 00:33:30,100
I want to know...

988
00:33:31,220 --> 00:33:32,160
how much longer they'll keep fighting.

989
00:33:32,180 --> 00:33:33,850
Forget your fortune.

990
00:33:33,870 --> 00:33:35,130
Look at my eyes first...

991
00:33:36,590 --> 00:33:38,330
They've been fighting all day.

992
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:39,400
Can I ask you something?

993
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:40,200
Mm.

994
00:33:40,710 --> 00:33:42,160
Dolly wants to see his father,

995
00:33:42,920 --> 00:33:44,120
but Dollar doesn't.

996
00:33:44,520 --> 00:33:45,380
What about you?

997
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:47,080
Do you want to see him?

998
00:33:48,540 --> 00:33:49,890
I don't know...

999
00:33:49,910 --> 00:33:51,710
It isn't important anymore.

1000
00:33:52,910 --> 00:33:54,900
I think

1001
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:58,510
the two people I want to wake up
and see every morning

1002
00:34:03,600 --> 00:34:05,620
are the ones arguing behind us.

1003
00:34:15,100 --> 00:34:16,239
Dollar, Dolly, my boys,

1004
00:34:16,260 --> 00:34:18,030
you can fight, you can bicker,

1005
00:34:18,040 --> 00:34:19,480
you can do whatever you want.

1006
00:34:21,150 --> 00:34:23,929
I know that deep down,

1007
00:34:23,949 --> 00:34:25,469
you two love each other.

1008
00:34:28,040 --> 00:34:29,570
But having you two...

1009
00:34:30,790 --> 00:34:31,880
in my life...

1010
00:34:34,020 --> 00:34:35,210
is more than enough.

1011
00:34:46,500 --> 00:34:47,159
Ow...

1012
00:34:47,179 --> 00:34:47,760
Ow...

1013
00:34:47,870 --> 00:34:48,560
- Boys.
- Hey!

1014
00:34:48,770 --> 00:34:49,370
Boys...

1015
00:34:49,389 --> 00:34:50,179
Yes?

1016
00:34:50,900 --> 00:34:51,719
Let's hug, alright?

1017
00:34:51,739 --> 00:34:52,820
Okay, Mom.

1018
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:54,199
Ow!

1019
00:34:54,219 --> 00:34:55,520
- Hey...
- Ow, ow.

1020
00:34:55,540 --> 00:34:56,330
Dawin,

1021
00:34:56,900 --> 00:34:58,120
- let's read my fortune.
- What? What?

1022
00:34:58,150 --> 00:34:59,550
- Dawin, read my... Ow!
- What?!

1023
00:34:59,580 --> 00:35:00,150
- Boys?
- What?!

1024
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:01,400
At ease!

1025
00:35:03,010 --> 00:35:03,510
Sit!

1026
00:35:04,780 --> 00:35:05,440
Hug!

1027
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:06,490
Hey!

1028
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:08,440
There, hug your brother.

1029
00:35:09,210 --> 00:35:10,010
Hug!

1030
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,220
Confess!

1031
00:35:16,940 --> 00:35:18,810
I'm sorry...

1032
00:35:18,830 --> 00:35:22,230
I... I love you very much.

1033
00:35:22,410 --> 00:35:23,860
I'm sorry, too.

1034
00:35:25,310 --> 00:35:27,120
Although you...

1035
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:29,180
are such an optimist...

1036
00:35:29,950 --> 00:35:30,950
Ow!

1037
00:35:30,980 --> 00:35:32,010
Why did you say that?

1038
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:32,640
Huh?!

1039
00:35:32,660 --> 00:35:33,790
Calm down.

1040
00:35:33,810 --> 00:35:35,160
Let me finish.

1041
00:35:36,210 --> 00:35:37,630
Although you...

1042
00:35:37,650 --> 00:35:39,490
are such an optimist,

1043
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:42,080
without you,

1044
00:35:42,090 --> 00:35:44,560
my world would be much darker.

1045
00:35:44,820 --> 00:35:48,410
If you hadn't made that sacrifice for me,

1046
00:35:48,430 --> 00:35:50,610
I probably wouldn't have graduated either.

1047
00:35:50,750 --> 00:35:52,090
It's okay, Daeng.

1048
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:53,460
Well...

1049
00:35:53,500 --> 00:35:55,030
I'm just dumb,

1050
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:56,590
so there's no point in spending money

1051
00:35:56,610 --> 00:35:57,540
to send me to school anyway.

1052
00:35:57,740 --> 00:35:58,740
Aw...

1053
00:36:02,810 --> 00:36:05,600
How can you be this cute, Dum?

1054
00:36:06,100 --> 00:36:08,490
My dear Moo Deng...

1055
00:36:10,370 --> 00:36:12,250
I love you so much, my Bie Sukrit.

1056
00:36:13,620 --> 00:36:15,120
It's that simple!

1057
00:36:15,140 --> 00:36:16,500
There's no need to fight!

1058
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:18,480
Wow!

1059
00:36:19,210 --> 00:36:21,280
You're amazing!

1060
00:36:21,500 --> 00:36:22,690
You can handle both Moo Deng

1061
00:36:22,710 --> 00:36:23,590
and Bie Sukrit!

1062
00:36:24,570 --> 00:36:25,800
Well done, tiger.

1063
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,970
Hey, what tiger?

1064
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,750
You said she was fierce
like a dog just the other day.

1065
00:36:30,760 --> 00:36:31,540
Dax...

1066
00:36:32,650 --> 00:36:33,540
It's true.

1067
00:36:34,200 --> 00:36:35,120
Like a dog?!

1068
00:36:35,140 --> 00:36:35,900
Who?!

1069
00:36:36,380 --> 00:36:37,510
Don't listen to him.

1070
00:36:37,530 --> 00:36:38,700
He's drunk. Talking nonsense.

1071
00:36:39,690 --> 00:36:41,060
I'm not talking nonsense.

1072
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:43,060
I still remember you saying,

1073
00:36:43,070 --> 00:36:44,610
"If you want a puppy,

1074
00:36:44,990 --> 00:36:46,090
you'll have to venture into a dog's den."

1075
00:36:46,110 --> 00:36:47,480
Hey, Dax!

1076
00:36:48,510 --> 00:36:49,110
Ow!

1077
00:36:49,150 --> 00:36:49,830
What?

1078
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:51,140
Dog's den, huh?!

1079
00:36:51,160 --> 00:36:52,330
You said, "a dog's den", huh?

1080
00:36:52,350 --> 00:36:54,010
Not just any dog, either.

1081
00:36:54,240 --> 00:36:55,240
Temple dogs.

1082
00:36:55,340 --> 00:36:56,520
Hey... Dax!

1083
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:58,430
Ow! When did I say that?

1084
00:36:58,490 --> 00:36:59,460
Temple dogs?!

1085
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:01,600
Dax!

1086
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:02,620
Shut your mouth! Ow!

1087
00:37:02,630 --> 00:37:03,650
Wait...no.
Looks like she won't hit me.

1088
00:37:03,890 --> 00:37:05,410
Hey, sit back down!

1089
00:37:05,430 --> 00:37:06,310
If you're drunk, go back to sleep!

1090
00:37:06,330 --> 00:37:07,640
- I'm not...
- You're not helping!

1091
00:37:08,010 --> 00:37:08,890
Everyone knows "Katy Perry."

1092
00:37:09,110 --> 00:37:09,750
But you're...

1093
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:11,080
a burden I have to "carry."

1094
00:37:11,340 --> 00:37:12,400
Go back to sleep. Go!

1095
00:37:12,660 --> 00:37:13,120
Sit!

1096
00:37:13,210 --> 00:37:13,780
Sit down!

1097
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:14,350
Quick!

1098
00:37:15,040 --> 00:37:15,820
Sleep!

1099
00:37:17,100 --> 00:37:18,080
You're not helping.

1100
00:37:18,300 --> 00:37:19,870
Hey, you don't have to listen to...

1101
00:37:20,950 --> 00:37:21,760
Ms. Danis?

1102
00:37:22,140 --> 00:37:23,010
Ms. Danis!

1103
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:25,140
Wow...

1104
00:37:25,270 --> 00:37:27,120
She's fierce, just like Grandpa said!

1105
00:37:29,100 --> 00:37:30,130
[Open]

1106
00:37:30,150 --> 00:37:31,260
[Closed]

1107
00:37:31,900 --> 00:37:32,900
Yes, Father.

1108
00:37:47,410 --> 00:37:48,620
Dang!

1109
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:51,330
It's a real Asian house gecko!

1110
00:37:51,500 --> 00:37:53,750
This is my first time seeing it.

1111
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:59,300
It must be nice, huh?

1112
00:38:00,240 --> 00:38:01,680
Hungry? Just eat bugs.

1113
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,240
Want to go somewhere? Just go.

1114
00:38:03,350 --> 00:38:05,000
Want to do something? Just do it.

1115
00:38:05,710 --> 00:38:06,710
You're free.

1116
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,300
You don't have to worry about
what other people think of you.

1117
00:38:13,710 --> 00:38:14,710
